    },
    {
      "id": "f2_ztext",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1720,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 681,
      "height": 280,
      "angle": 0,
      "autoResize": true,
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "boundElements": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "frameId": null,
      "groupIds": [],
      "index": "a52",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "opacity": 100,
      "originalText": "connector_loader.rb:127-132   avatar_cache_key(file_hash, file, base_dir)\n\n  no sibling SVGs:  key = file_hash                              (line 129)\n  with SVGs:        key = SHA256(file_hash,\n                                File.basename(base_dir), fingerprint)  (line 132)\n\nfile_hash is the SHA256 of the connector's bytes (line 77).\nNeither form contains the directory. Therefore\n  lib/connectors/debug_connector/debug_connector.rb\n  <checkout>/connectors/debug_connector/debug_connector.rb\nshare one key whenever their bytes match, and getset (line 82)\nreturns whichever copy was parsed FIRST, procs and their\nsource_location included.\n\nThe cache exists to skip re-parsing identical connectors. It also,\nunintentionally, decides which file the importer will later copy.",
      "roughness": 1,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 15670717,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "text": "connector_loader.rb:127-132   avatar_cache_key(file_hash, file, base_dir)\n\n  no sibling SVGs:  key = file_hash                              (line 129)\n  with SVGs:        key = SHA256(file_hash,\n                                File.basename(base_dir), fingerprint)  (line 132)\n\nfile_hash is the SHA256 of the connector's bytes (line 77).\nNeither form contains the directory. Therefore\n  lib/connectors/debug_connector/debug_connector.rb\n  <checkout>/connectors/debug_connector/debug_connector.rb\nshare one key whenever their bytes match, and getset (line 82)\nreturns whichever copy was parsed FIRST, procs and their\nsource_location included.\n\nThe cache exists to skip re-parsing identical connectors. It also,\nunintentionally, decides which file the importer will later copy.",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "updated": 1788682975226,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 2009784847,
      "verticalAlign": "middle"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2_etext",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1720,
      "y": 690,
      "width": 639,
      "height": 175,
      "angle": 0,
      "autoResize": true,
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "boundElements": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "frameId": null,
      "groupIds": [],
      "index": "a53",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "opacity": 100,
      "originalText": "seed 22 clean run: 4481 examples, 9 failures, all Errno::ENOENT on that path\n  (indexes 2747-2749 importer, 3074-3079 cloner)\nconnector_importer_spec alone: 7/7, also under --order rand:22\n  (same order inside the file)\nimporter after the cloner, the loader, or the job_state spec, one process\n  each: all green. So no single second file reproduces it.\ninstrumented replay (gate/hooks/trace_connector_location.rb): the\n  registry's debug connector source path flips lib/ → checkout right\n  after job_state_read_isolation_spec[1:2:2] and never flips back\nthe example behind moment 1 is not pinned; neither fix needs it",
      "roughness": 1,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 974090340,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "text": "seed 22 clean run: 4481 examples, 9 failures, all Errno::ENOENT on that path\n  (indexes 2747-2749 importer, 3074-3079 cloner)\nconnector_importer_spec alone: 7/7, also under --order rand:22\n  (same order inside the file)\nimporter after the cloner, the loader, or the job_state spec, one process\n  each: all green. So no single second file reproduces it.\ninstrumented replay (gate/hooks/trace_connector_location.rb): the\n  registry's debug connector source path flips lib/ → checkout right\n  after job_state_read_isolation_spec[1:2:2] and never flips back\nthe example behind moment 1 is not pinned; neither fix needs it",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "updated": 1788682975226,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1205038638,
      "verticalAlign": "middle"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2_fixtext",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1720,
      "y": 1070,
      "width": 714,
      "height": 263,
      "angle": 0,
      "autoResize": true,
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "boundElements": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "frameId": null,
      "groupIds": [],
      "index": "a54",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "opacity": 100,
      "originalText": "Not the key. Putting base_dir into the key removed the 9 failures but broke\nconnector_loader_avatar_spec.rb:109 and connector_loader_spec.rb:188, which\nguard cross-path cache sharing as a designed feature. Retracted.\n\nThe defect is in the consumer. connector_importer.rb:109-114 turns a\ncache-chosen copy's proc.source_location into the file to copy and never\nchecks that it still exists. The fix, 10 lines in the same method:\n  return the path if File.exist?(path); otherwise fall back to the canonical\n  copy from ConnectorLoader.connector_rb_paths_under(lib/connectors)\n  (the same lookup application.rb:107 uses), else raise a clear error.\n\nValidated in the gate worktree with key-cache clears (finding 1):\n  fast gate: importer + both cache guards + degrade + cloner = 85/85\n  full seed 22 replay: 4481 examples, 0 failures, 16.9 min\nPatch saved at ~/personal/scripts/gate/hooks/connector_importer_source_location.patch",
      "roughness": 1,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1095203812,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "text": "Not the key. Putting base_dir into the key removed the 9 failures but broke\nconnector_loader_avatar_spec.rb:109 and connector_loader_spec.rb:188, which\nguard cross-path cache sharing as a designed feature. Retracted.\n\nThe defect is in the consumer. connector_importer.rb:109-114 turns a\ncache-chosen copy's proc.source_location into the file to copy and never\nchecks that it still exists. The fix, 10 lines in the same method:\n  return the path if File.exist?(path); otherwise fall back to the canonical\n  copy from ConnectorLoader.connector_rb_paths_under(lib/connectors)\n  (the same lookup application.rb:107 uses), else raise a clear error.\n\nValidated in the gate worktree with key-cache clears (finding 1):\n  fast gate: importer + both cache guards + degrade + cloner = 85/85\n  full seed 22 replay: 4481 examples, 0 failures, 16.9 min\nPatch saved at ~/personal/scripts/gate/hooks/connector_importer_source_location.patch",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "updated": 1788684497505,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 621643950,
      "verticalAlign": "middle"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2_ctext",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1720,
      "y": 1430,
      "width": 580,
      "height": 210,
      "angle": 0,
      "autoResize": true,
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "boundElements": null,
      "containerId": null,
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "frameId": null,
      "groupIds": [],
      "index": "a55",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "opacity": 100,
      "originalText": "ConnectorLoader.connector_cache.clear in a global before(:each)\n(connector_loader_spec.rb:6 already does it for its own examples)\nremoves all 9 failures BUT breaks solution_loader_degrade_spec.rb:237\n'degrades every runbook, not just the first few, when the breaches\ncost real time': it stubs ProcHelper#execute_if_valid to sleep 1\n(line 240) and expects every runbook unresolved. With a cold cache\nthe stub also fires while the connectors themselves parse, the\nrequest budget is spent before runbook 2, and the later runbooks\ncome back 'not_attempted' instead of 'field_logic_unresolved'.\n\n26/26 alone · 1 failure with the clear · loader then degrade 48/48\n(so today's suite is safe; a blanket clear would not be)",
      "roughness": 1,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1923997940,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "text": "ConnectorLoader.connector_cache.clear in a global before(:each)\n(connector_loader_spec.rb:6 already does it for its own examples)\nremoves all 9 failures BUT breaks solution_loader_degrade_spec.rb:237\n'degrades every runbook, not just the first few, when the breaches\ncost real time': it stubs ProcHelper#execute_if_valid to sleep 1\n(line 240) and expects every runbook unresolved. With a cold cache\nthe stub also fires while the connectors themselves parse, the\nrequest budget is spent before runbook 2, and the later runbooks\ncome back 'not_attempted' instead of 'field_logic_unresolved'.\n\n26/26 alone · 1 failure with the clear · loader then degrade 48/48\n(so today's suite is safe; a blanket clear would not be)",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "updated": 1788684523663,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 42089422,
      "verticalAlign": "middle"
    },
